===Useful Powershell Commands===

>General Commands
	Clear	or CTRL+L							clear screen
	Get-Verb								get a list of ps commands
	Get-Help
	Get-Help out-file							help on specific topic

>Output Formatting
	Format-Table								
	Out-GridView								uses GUI to display output, includes filters
	Out-File								output to the file
	Convert-ToCsv | Out-File -File Path [C:\..]

>Examining Processes
	Get-Process		                    				get info about running processes
    	Get-Process 'power*'           						get info about named process with wildcard
	Get-Process -Name powershell						get info about named process
	Get-Process -Id 1234							get info about process with PID 1234
    	Get-Process 'powershell' | Select-Object *    				get detailled (all objects) info about a named process
	Get-Process  Computer-Name SEC504STUDENT            			get info about running processes on a remote system
	Get-Process | Get-Member						lists all properties available for a command
	Get-Process | Select-Object -Property *					lists all properties of all processes
	Get-Process | Select-Object -Property Name,Id,Path			lists selected properties (Name, ID, Path) of all processes
	
	Get-Process | Select-Object -Property Path, Name, Id | Where-Object -Property Name -eq explorer
										lists selected properties (Name, ID, Path) of the processes which name is "explorer"

	Get-Process | Select-Object -Property Path, Name, Id | Where-Object -Property Path -Like "*temp*"
										lists selected properties (Name, ID, Path) of the processes which path contains "temp"

	Get-CimInstance -Class Win32_Process					lists processes with the class tyme win32 process
	Get-CimInstance -Class Win32_Process | Select-Object -Property *	lists full details of all processes with the class tyme win32 process

	Get-CimInstance -Class Win32_Process | Select-Object -Property Name, Path, ProcessId, ParentProcessId	
										lists full selected details of all processes with the class tyme win32 process
	Get-CimInstance -Class Win32_Process | Where-Object -Property ParentProcessId -eq 123			
										lists full details of the process with Parent PID 123
